  "result": "Excellent! All 184 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 \"Only issued or partially_paid invoices can be paid.\"\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 \"Payment exceeds the amount owed.\"\n\n**Created src/payments.js:**\n\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` \u2014 records a payment and updates invoice\n  - Only works on 'issued' or 'partially_paid' invoices (returns NOT_ISSUED otherwise)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID if not)\n  - Prevents overpayment (returns OVERPAYMENT if amount exceeds what's owed)\n  - Creates payments array if missing\n  - Updates status: 'paid' when payments cover the total, 'partially_paid' otherwise\n  - Never mutates the input invoice\n\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 calculates remaining amount owed\n  - Returns total minus sum of payments\n  - Clamped at 0 (never goes negative)\n\n**Added 17 comprehensive tests to test/payments.test.js:**\n- Single and multiple payment recording\n- Status transitions (partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error validation (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, OVERPAYMENT)\n- Edge cases: zero/negative/fractional amounts, overpayment scenarios\n- Input immutability\n- balanceDue calculations at various payment states\n\nAll tests pass and the implementation maintains the no-mutation rule throughout, properly calculating balances through invoiceTotals and payment summation.",
